# v0.8.3 PATCH — `acs-verified` gate accepts REMOVED as a non-failure verdict

2026-05-13. Sealed local; awaiting dispatcher dogfood publish per
ASK-FIRST. v0.8.3 closes the third orthogonal `check_acs_verified`
defect surfaced by the v0.9.0 paper publish flow (first two were
v0.7.2 §4-scoping + v0.8.2 `--plan-doc` flag).

The defect: the `check_acs_verified` verdict-loop recognises only
`GREEN` as a pass token via `re.escape(ac) + r".{0,240}?GREEN"`.
When an AC is legitimately struck mid-build per ODD §4 re-extension
(the paper publish's AC.ODDPAPER.3 was REMOVED at build-time per
D-ODDPAPER.5.2 Path C — stale HTML couldn't be regenerated, so the
HTML-rendering AC was dropped; markdown-only ship), the §status
verdict matrix records `| AC.ODDPAPER.3 | REMOVED | Build-time
D-ODDPAPER.5.2 ... |` instead of GREEN. The gate flagged the AC as
missing-from-§status and RED'd the publish despite a structurally
complete build.

The fix is a narrow extension to the verdict-loop: before adding
an AC to the `missing` list, also try the REMOVED proximity-pattern
(`re.escape(ac) + r".{0,240}?REMOVED"`). If either GREEN or
REMOVED matches within 240 chars, the AC counts as verified.
Missing-verdict (no recognised pass token near AC ID) still
returns RED — the fix doesn't open the gate to silently-skipped
ACs.

REMOVED encodes ODD §4 re-extension as a recognised build-time
outcome per `feedback_locked_design_not_license_for_bad_outcomes`:
locked design IS revisitable mid-build when empirical reality
contradicts it; the discipline is that the revision must be named
in the plan-doc (D-`<plan-id>.<n>` reference). The gate's job is
verdict recognition; verdict-justification verification stays
plan-doc-author + reviewer responsibility (D-RVG.2.b).

